Run standalone assembly, iterate diff analysis across implementations, replay saved testcases, or emit build artifacts without executing them.

Usage: DRVFuzz <COMMAND>

Commands:
  exec           Execute one assembly program on a selected implementation
  diff           Iteratively fuzz multiple implementations and minimize divergences
  diff-testcase  Replay diff analysis from an existing testcase
  diff-spike     Compare Spike against other implementations for the configured ISA
  generate       Generate a random testcase and ELF artifacts without executing
  help           Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

===== exec --help
Compile and run the provided assembly for the chosen implementation and ISA base. Writes execution_output.json, execution_report.md, and instruction snapshots under the run directory for later inspection.

Usage: DRVFuzz exec [OPTIONS] --asm <ASM> --riscv-impl <RISCV_IMPL> --isa <ISA> --run-dir <RUN_DIR>

Options:
      --asm <ASM>
          Assembly file containing the initialization and test instructions to execute

      --riscv-impl <RISCV_IMPL>
          Implementation wrapper to run against (e.g. spike, rocket, picorv32, cva6)
          
          [possible values: spike, rocket, boom-v3, boom-v4, pico-rv32, cva6, xiang-shan, ibex, vex, kronos, srv32]

      --isa <ISA>
          ISA base to assemble for (rv32 or rv64)
          
          [possible values: rv32, rv64]

      --run-dir <RUN_DIR>
          Directory where artifacts are written; a per-implementation subdirectory is created

      --timeout-secs <TIMEOUT_SECS>
          Optional execution timeout in seconds; omit to let the run complete naturally

      --allow-unaligned
          Request unaligned memory accesses if the implementation supports them

      --transition-report
          Emit transition_report.json/.md using SDModel execution-state transitions

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

===== diff --help
Continuously generates random programs from the provided testcase_config, executes them across the selected implementations, and minimizes any mismatching behavior. Each worker writes a timestamped subdirectory under --run-dir. Leave --max-runs unset to keep iterating until a worker fails or you stop the process.

Usage: DRVFuzz diff [OPTIONS] --testcase-config <TESTCASE_CONFIG> --run-dir <RUN_DIR>

Options:
      --testcase-config <TESTCASE_CONFIG>
          TOML file containing the [testcase_config] used to generate random programs

      --riscv-impl [<RISCV_IMPLS>...]
          Implementations to include; defaults to every ISA-compatible core, filtered by unaligned_access_required
          
          [possible values: spike, rocket, boom-v3, boom-v4, pico-rv32, cva6, xiang-shan, ibex, vex, kronos, srv32]

      --impl-timeout <IMPL_TIMEOUT_FILE>
          TOML file with an [impl_timeout_secs] table mapping implementations to per-run timeouts (seconds)

      --run-options <RUN_OPTIONS_FILE>
          TOML file providing diff runner options (iterations, emit, cleanup); supports flat or [run_options] formats

      --run-dir <RUN_DIR>
          Base directory for diff runs; each iteration gets a timestamped subdirectory

      --concurrency <CONCURRENCY>
          Number of diff-analysis workers to run in parallel
          
          [default: 1]

      --max-runs <MAX_RUNS>
          Total diff iterations to execute across all workers; omit to keep running until stopped

      --sdmodel
          Enable the SDModel sensitive-data generator for boundary values and exception triggers

      --sdmodel-probability <SDMODEL_PROBABILITY>
          Override SDModel injection probability (0.0 to 1.0)

      --transition-guided
          Enable transition-guided seed feedback using SDModel execution states

      --mode-guided
          Enable mode-guided ablation feedback using individual SDModel states only

      --transition-seed-pool-limit <TRANSITION_SEED_POOL_LIMIT>
          Maximum number of transition-interesting seeds retained

      --transition-seed-window <TRANSITION_SEED_WINDOW>
          Number of seed test instructions spliced into each guided testcase

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

===== diff-spike --help
For each selected implementation that supports the configured ISA base, run the diff-analysis workflow between Spike and that target. Artifacts are written under --run-dir/spike_<impl>_<isa>. Defaults to testing Spike against every supported implementation.

Usage: DRVFuzz diff-spike [OPTIONS] --testcase-config <TESTCASE_CONFIG> --run-dir <RUN_DIR>

Options:
      --testcase-config <TESTCASE_CONFIG>
          TOML file containing the [testcase_config] used to generate random programs

      --run-dir <RUN_DIR>
          Base directory used to store run artifacts for each Spike pairing (subdirectories are created automatically)

      --concurrency <CONCURRENCY>
          Number of diff-analysis workers to run in parallel for each pairing
          
          [default: 1]

      --max-runs <MAX_RUNS>
          Total diff-analysis runs to execute per pairing; omit to keep iterating

      --riscv-impl [<RISCV_IMPLS>...]
          Optional list of non-Spike implementations to pair with Spike; defaults to all ISA-compatible targets
          
          [possible values: spike, rocket, boom-v3, boom-v4, pico-rv32, cva6, xiang-shan, ibex, vex, kronos, srv32]

      --impl-timeout <IMPL_TIMEOUT_FILE>
          TOML file with an [impl_timeout_secs] table mapping implementations to per-run timeouts (seconds)

      --run-options <RUN_OPTIONS_FILE>
          TOML file providing diff runner options (iterations, emit, cleanup); supports flat or [run_options] formats

      --sdmodel
          Enable the SDModel sensitive-data generator for boundary values and exception triggers

      --sdmodel-probability <SDMODEL_PROBABILITY>
          Override SDModel injection probability (0.0 to 1.0)

      --transition-guided
          Enable transition-guided seed feedback using SDModel execution states

      --mode-guided
          Enable mode-guided ablation feedback using individual SDModel states only

      --transition-seed-pool-limit <TRANSITION_SEED_POOL_LIMIT>
          Maximum number of transition-interesting seeds retained

      --transition-seed-window <TRANSITION_SEED_WINDOW>
          Number of seed test instructions spliced into each guided testcase

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
